# CTL-SOV01 -- W4-MC-07: control-level check of Soviet mission 1 through the
# REAL shell with REAL clicks / touch gestures only (no cheats, no centring).
# The original's opening: input locked, the start scroll, then control.
set render_every 0
set on_quit continue

click button "Single Player"
click button "New Campaign"
require scene == "shell:Campaign"
click well:soviet
click button Load
until 30 scene == campaign-load
until 300 scene == game
require scene == game
until 60 input_locked == 1                    @W4-MC-02
shot t0
until 1200 input_locked == 0                  @W4-MC-02
wait 5
assert ctl_units >= 5                         @W4-MC-07
assert ctl_on_screen >= 1                     @W4-MC-07
shot unlocked

# --- band select whatever of ours is on screen, order a move ----------------------
# (`:near` = the E2 nearest the selection: since the w5-camp merge the first E2
# of the list walks off-screen during the opening, a player clicks one he sees)
drag xy 30 30 1080 690                        @W4-MC-07
wait 1
assert selected >= 1                          @W4-MC-07
let n = selected
# w7 (fv7a): with the original speeds the opening walk-in ends later and its
# crowd (and SOV01's hostile civilians) fill the cells around the conscript --
# +2 +2 landed on a civilian (an attack order), so aim at a free cell and
# check the cursor first that the click IS a move order.
# (fv8a: since w8fix-save's paradrop missions (one jump per 5-frame Overfly
# tick, FUN_00415960/00415C60; bisected 2f12df9 PASS / 587a5b4 FAIL) the opening crowd gathers in a
# different crowd and +2 -2 is a conscript (the select cursor): +4 -4.)
move unit 0:E2:near +4 -4 onscreen
assert cursor_name == move                    @W4-MC-07
click unit 0:E2:near +4 -4 onscreen                @W4-MC-07
wait 1
assert sel_moving >= 1                        @W4-MC-07
wait 45

# --- the same by touch: one-finger scroll, tap-select, tap-move ---------------------
# W6-01-06: a tap on a unit of a selected army is an order, so deselect first
# (two-finger tap) to make the next tap a select.
# (`:near` needs a selection: tap a conscript before the deselect, which with
# the army selected is an order to its cell, then deselect and select it.)
touch tap unit 0:E2:near onscreen                  @W6-01-06
wait 1
assert selected == $n                         @W6-01-06
touch pan2 xy 400 300 400 300
wait 1
assert selected == 0
touch tap unit 0:E2                                @W4-MC-07
wait 1
assert selected == 1
# (fv7a: -2 +2 is now an impassable cell here (NoMove) and the E2 was still
# walking from the army order, a hollow pass -- tap a cell the cursor shows as
# a move.)
# (fv8a: the post-paradrop crowd covers +2 +2 too -- +4 +4.)
move unit 0:E2:near +4 +4 onscreen
assert cursor_name == move                    @W4-MC-07
touch tap unit 0:E2:near +4 +4 onscreen            @W4-MC-07
wait 1
assert sel_moving >= 1                        @W4-MC-07
let cx0 = cam_x
touch drag xy 520 300 400 300                 @W4-AM-01
wait 1
assert cam_x == $cx0-120                      @W4-AM-01
assert selected == 1                          @W4-AM-01
shot moved
assert outcome == RUNNING
end
